<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australian Sept export prices fall 1.6 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australian Sept export prices fall 1.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-11-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian export prices fell 1.6 percent in September from the previous month and were 4.4 percent lower than September 1995, the Australian Bureau Statistics said on Friday.  </p>
<p>&quot;An increase in the value of the Australian dollar against the major trading currencies led to price falls in a wide range of items in September,&quot; the bureau said in a statement.</p>
<p>The monthly rate for export prices has been negative for most of this year, but the annual rate has now risen from a trough of 7.6 percent in July.</p>
<p>-- Canberra Bureau 61-6 273-2730</p>
</text>
